course: dictionary
lesson: 1447
title: Naming the person who draws
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cartoonist is a person who draws cartoons. Look at the parts of the word: cartoon is the drawing, and -ist often means a person who does a job or activity, like a dentist or a artist.
explain: Cartoons can be funny or simple drawings, comic strips, or animated films. «Cartoonists often draw four fingers because it is quicker and looks neater.» A cartoonist uses simple shapes instead of real detail, so the picture is quick to draw and easy to read.
explain: Some cartoonists draw for newspapers. Their political cartoons comment on news and leaders, and they can be funny and make serious points at the same time.
fact: A cartoonist is a person who draws cartoons.
fact: A cartoon can be a funny or simple drawing, a comic strip, or an animated film.
fact: «Cartoonists» is the plural, and means more than one cartoonist.
fact: Political cartoonists draw for newspapers and make a point about news or politics.
fact: Charles Schulz (Peanuts) and Hergé (Tintin) were famous cartoonists.
exercise: What does a cartoonist do? | *Draws cartoons: funny or simple drawings, comic strips, or animated films | Takes photographs of cats for a magazine | Writes the weather report on the radio
exercise: «Cartoonists often draw four fingers because it is quicker and looks neater.» Why do cartoonists draw four fingers? | *Because it is quicker and looks neater | Because four is their favourite number | Because real hands have only four fingers | Because they cannot fit five fingers on the page
exercise: Charles Schulz (Peanuts) and Hergé (Tintin) were famous for which job? | *Cartoonists | Gardeners | Pilots | Bakers
test: Find and copy the word in «Cartoonists often draw four fingers» that names the job. | *Cartoonists | draw | four | fingers
test: What is a political cartoonist most likely to draw for? | A bedroom wall | A shoe shop window | A school sports day | *A newspaper, to comment on news or politics
exam: Political cartoons can be funny, and they can also do what? | Show only animals | *Make serious points about news and leaders | Sell shoes in a shop | Stop people from reading
